     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It has puzzled me for awhile why .csv files don&#39;t show up when I use the fileInput component on Windows. I think it&#39;s better to add &quot;.csv,&quot; to the list of accepts otherwise the component doesn&#39;t show the csv files, like so<div><br></div><div>&lt;input id=&quot;file1&quot; type=&quot;file&quot; accept=&quot;<b>.csv,</b>text/csv,text/comma-separated-values,text/plain,csv,csv&quot;/&gt;<br></div><div><br></div><div>Not sure if this has to do with Microsoft Excel being installed.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/11832930/html-input-file-accept-attribute-file-type-csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/11832930/html-input-file-accept-attribute-file-type-csv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792406928865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw34GUQIThATTH3G08de2Mtj\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/11832930/html-input-file-accept-attribute-file-type-csv</a></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
